<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ivane Mkhargrdzeli</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1227</span> · Also known as Ivane Zakarian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ivane <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zakarids">Mkhargrdzeli</a> was a Georgian-Armenian noble and general of the Zakarid family who, with his brother Zakare, commanded the armies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamar-of-georgia">Queen Tamar</a>. Together they won the victories of Shamkor in 1195 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-basiani">Basiani</a> around 1202 and conquered much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a>, which the family governed. Ivane later became atabeg and a leading figure at court under George IV and Rusudan, and he converted from Armenian to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgian-orthodox-church">Georgian Orthodoxy</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ivane-mkhargrdzeli.jpg" alt="Ivane Mkhargrdzeli" width="320" height="621" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jacgroumo · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ivane_at_Harichavank.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
